<WikiLayout title="WARDOGS Weapon Compare" description="Compare WARDOGS weapon roles and open version-bound entity references." canonicalPath="/tools/weapon-compare/" pageType="WebApplication" showAd={true} adPlacement="tool">
  <p class="eyebrow">TOOL / WEAPONS</p><h1>Weapon Compare</h1><p>Compare two weapons by role before opening their full references. This prevents a single unsupported number from standing in for range, positioning and loadout context.</p><ToolShell tool="Weapon comparison" description="Select two weapons for a quick role comparison. Detailed values remain on their entity pages." leftLabel="Weapon A" rightLabel="Weapon B" options={['M4','AK74','RPG-7','MAAWS','Mosin-Nagant','SV98']}/><div class="inline-link-row"><a href="/database/weapons/">Weapons database</a><a href="/weapons/builds/">Weapon builds</a></div>
  <section><h2>Comparison method</h2><p>Start with class and intended task. A general-purpose rifle and an anti-vehicle launcher solve different problems, so they should not be reduced to one ranking. Open both entity records to compare combat role, effective usage, strengths, weaknesses and related loadout guidance.</p><h2>Confirmed and unconfirmed data</h2><p>The tool does not manufacture damage, recoil or attachment values. When reliable evidence is unavailable, the value remains <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>. Check the <a href="/sources/">source policy</a> for how version-sensitive claims are handled.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What to review after comparing</h2><p>Check whether both selections fit the same engagement range and battlefield task. Then review ammunition planning, supporting utility and replacement risk as part of the complete loadout. A weapon that is appropriate for one position may be inefficient when the objective moves or the squad needs anti-vehicle support instead. The <a href="/loadouts/">Loadouts hub</a> connects those choices to role-based planning.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Does the comparison declare a winner?</h3><p>No. It helps identify which option better matches the intended scenario.</p><h3>Where are full weapon details?</h3><p>Open the <a href="/database/weapons/">Weapons Database</a> and follow the entity link for each selection.</p><p><a href="/compare/">Browse evidence-aware weapon comparison pages →</a></p></section>
</WikiLayout>
